# DF STARTUP-INVINCIBILITY CONTACT rig (14z-126) — does the hit test HONOUR
# the window the per-character seq-0x16 handler arms in +0x147?
#
# Static reading (14z-126, vsavj opcode view): the shared DF activation body
# PRG:0x027000 arms only the THROW invulnerability (+0x143 = 0x14); the
# INVINCIBILITY timer +0x147 is armed by the PER-CHARACTER handler that
# dispatch_16 (PRG:0x0BF31A) selects for seq 0x16 — Bulleta/Demitri 0x29,
# Victor 0x3B, ... — decremented by the System Timer Reducer PRG:0x02246E and
# tested on the VICTIM (a1) by the hit test at PRG:0x018064. The tenants' rows
# are repointed to their own vs2 handlers (Donovan 0x40, Huitzil 0x4F, Pyron
# 0x29). This replay is the LIVE half: the same attack landing INSIDE the window
# must not touch P1's HP, and landing OUTSIDE it must.
#
# Runs UNCHANGED on any vsavj-based build; the character under test is chosen
# by POKES (the replay-85 doctrine):
#   P1 $FF8782 = character under test (01 Demitri legacy; 13/11/10 tenants)
#   P2 $FF8B82 = 0x03 Victor — the attacker, same id on both games
#   P1 $FF8509 = 3 banked stocks before each activation (the seq-0x0A trap)
#   x pins at t-230 (the `far` pin of tools/name_moves.py: P1 552, P2 728),
#   then P2 WALKS IN for 150 frames — a near pair is never poked (14z-120 (2))
#   P1 HP re-pinned to 0x120/0x120 at t-20 before each event ([VSP-125] shape)
#
# EVENT 1 (IN, t=3260): P1 activates (HP+HK) at t; Victor presses HP at t+4,
#   which lands ~t+12..t+16 — inside every window the table arms (>= 41 f).
# EVENT 2 (OUT, t=4260): the same, Victor pressing at t+110 — after the
#   longest window (Huitzil 79 f) and the throw invulnerability (20 f).
# A leg whose attack never FIRED (P2's node never enters a Victor 5HP chain)
# is UNMEASURED, never "invulnerable" ([VSE-76], [VSP-137]).
300-305 sys=C1
420-425 sys=C2
800-803 sys=S1
940-943 sys=S2
